WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.276
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.512 --> 00:00:06.970
SPEAKER: In this
video, we're going

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:09.262
to walk through how to update
your Google Cloud Billing

00:00:09.262 --> 00:00:11.200
Account and Payments
Profile settings

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.180
for self-serve accounts.

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:16.300
Your Billing Account and
Payments Profile work together.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.040
The Billing Account
tracks the costs

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.870
incurred by all
attached projects

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:22.750
and defines who pays
for the resources.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.240
It is connected to a
Payments Profile, which

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:27.370
stores your payment
instrument information

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:29.980
and defines how you
pay for charges.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.200
Both your Billing Account
and Payments Profile

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.600
store several pieces
of information.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.300
For the selection of items
highlighted in this video,

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.060
some can be changed after
initial creation and some

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:41.770
cannot.

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:43.690
To change those
items, you will need

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:46.990
to create a new Billing Account
and/or Payments Profile.

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:49.660
We will now cover how to
update changeable items

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:51.280
using the Cloud Console.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.980
Get started by heading
into the Console.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:57.550
Then head to the Navigation
menu in the left-hand pane.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:00.880
Choose Billing, then
use the dropdown menu

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:03.310
to select Manage
Billing Accounts.

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:05.200
First, we will walk
through changes

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.280
that can be made to a
Cloud Billing Account,

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:09.670
including display
name and organization.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:12.160
In order to perform
these tasks, you'll

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:14.860
need to be a Billing Account
Administrator on the Billing

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:16.590
Account.

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.900
Select the Billing Account
you want to update.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:21.240
This will open
the Overview page.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:24.450
In the left-hand nav,
choose Account Management.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.760
At the top of the window,
you will find the option

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:29.040
to change the organization.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:32.440
You will also see an option
to rename the Billing Account.

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:35.100
This name is what users see
displayed on the console

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:39.660
when enabling or changing
billing on projects.

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:41.270
Next, we will walk
through changes

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:43.220
that can be made to
a Payments Profile,

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:46.190
including billing address,
payment users, and payment

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:47.300
method.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:50.030
A Payments Profile can be linked
to multiple payment accounts

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:53.270
across Google products, such as
Google Workspace, Google Cloud,

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:55.530
Google Ads, and more.

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:57.360
So keep in mind that
changes will apply

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.460
to all linked payment accounts.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:03.580
In the left-hand nav,
click Payment Settings.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:05.620
In the Payments
Profile section, you

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:08.889
will see an option to update
the business name and address.

00:02:08.889 --> 00:02:11.890
This mailing address is the
legally registered business

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:14.770
address that gets
printed on invoices.

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:16.630
In order to change
the billing address,

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:19.840
you must have Edit Payment
Profile permission or Admin

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:23.380
With All Permissions for
the Payments Profile.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:25.870
Note that permissions
for the Payments Profile

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:29.170
are set by visiting
pay.google.com and not using

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:31.720
the Google Cloud IAM service.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.930
Next, scroll down to the
Payments User section.

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:37.660
Follow the link to
Manage Payments Users,

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:39.760
where you can add,
delete, and update

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:42.610
payment user details,
including contact information

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:44.740
and notification settings.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:46.990
In order to perform
these tasks, you

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:49.210
must have the Manage
Users permission,

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:52.390
or for full capabilities, the
Admin With All Permissions

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:54.820
role for the Payments Profile.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:56.860
Finally, to update
the payment method,

00:02:56.860 --> 00:03:00.640
navigate to the Payment Method
page using the left-hand nav.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:03.190
Here you can update your
primary payment method

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:05.140
and add new payment methods.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:07.060
In order to manage
payment methods,

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.850
you must be an admin with all
permissions for the Payments

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:10.870
Profile.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:13.900
Head over to the documentation
to check out more details.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:17.250
[MUSIC PLAYING]

